[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hello,<br>\nI've been fighting with the elaborator for a while now, and I think I'm kinda close to generating a structure with like a given amount of fields of some given types, but I can't quite get there.<br>\nI have something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fields</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TSyntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Lean.Parser.Command.structFields</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">structFields</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">fields</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cmd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">structName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">typeBinders</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">fields</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But I get this error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Application</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mismatch</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">The</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">argument</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fields</span>\n<span class=\"n\">has</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">TSyntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Lean.Parser.Command.structFields</span>\n<span class=\"n\">but</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">TSyntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Lean.Parser.Command.structCtor</span>\n<span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">application</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fields</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Which kinda makes sense. How can I work around this? Or is there a simpler way of constructing a structure dynamically?<br>\nThanks!</p>",
        "id": 630280032,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1791498463
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>what if you write <code>$fields:structFields</code></p>",
        "id": 630280860,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1791498812
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, that works. I even used that trick in some code segment before that already <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 630281042,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1791498887
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The whole code still feels extremely hacky though. Like why do I need to parse structSimpleBinders for the dynamically generated fields but then later on throw structFields at it again when combining the fields? Does it just parse everything twice then?</p>",
        "id": 630281255,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1791498997
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Are there maybe some examples of code like the exemplary one above?</p>",
        "id": 630281377,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1791499048
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>the parsing is done at compile time, at runtime it just constructs the syntax</p>",
        "id": 630281385,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1791499050
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So fighting with the smaller parsers is expected when dynamically building up larger structures (pun not intended) like the code needed for a structure?</p>",
        "id": 630281623,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1791499145
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can you give a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a>?</p>",
